@startuml

title The step protocol: the participants and the messages between them

skinparam componentStyle rectangle

package "the client" {
    [caller] as caller
    [reader] as reader
}

package "the platform" {
    [workflow engine\n(the process manager)] as engine
    [definition] as definition
    [step handler\n(an operation)] as handler
    database "the run state" as state
}

caller --> engine : publish the start message\n(the caller names the instance,\nand is answered before the run finishes)

engine --> definition : build the step list\n(from the run's stored request alone,\nthe same list on every advance)

engine --> handler : publish the step command\n(the step, the instance and the tenant;\nno caller token)

handler --> engine : publish the completion event\n(complete, warn or fail\nfor the step the command named)

engine --> state : record the run and its steps\n(the process manager's record\nof every outcome)

engine --> handler : publish the retry verb\n(stop the run on the failed step,\nthen re-dispatch it)

reader --> state : read the progress\n(the caller follows the run rather than waiting)

@enduml
